# file-mcp-server Docker Deployment Guide

This guide covers image build, certs, runtime configuration, deployment modes, server control, and Docker-specific tests.

## 1. Build the image

```bash
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

With custom CA for build-time TLS trust:

```bash
CUSTOM_CA_CERT=/path/to/enterprise-ca.crt \
HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Direct Docker build:

```bash
docker buildx build --load --network=host -t cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest .
```

## 2. Runtime files and mounts

Prepare runtime directories and env:

```bash
mkdir -p run/workspace run/logs certs
cp docker-env.example run/env.base
```

Container mount strategy:
- `run/workspace` -> file scope root and operational storage
- `run/logs` -> audit/server logs and snapshots
- `certs` -> optional CA bundle(s)
- env files -> mounted into `/workspace/*.env`

## 3. Single-config run (host network)

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/app/config.yaml \
  -e FILE_MCP_DEFAULTS_PATH=/app/defaults.yaml \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Health check:

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

## 4. Multi-configuration run (layered env files)

`file_mcp_server` supports comma-separated env file paths. Use this to keep base + environment overlays.

Example:

```bash
cat > run/env.prod <<'ENV'
FILE_MCP_API_KEY_PRIMARY=prod-secret
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/workspace
FILE_MCP_AUDIT_LOG=/workspace/logs/audit.log.jsonl
FILE_MCP_SERVER_LOG=/workspace/logs/server.log
FILE_MCP_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/workspace/logs/snapshots
FILE_MCP_HTTP_TRANSPORT=streamable-http
FILE_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
FILE_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8000
FILE_MCP_HTTP_BASE_PATH=/
FILE_MCP_HTTP_MCP_PATH=/mcp
FILE_MCP_HTTP_HEALTH_PATH=/health
FILE_MCP_HTTP_EVENTS_PATH=/events
FILE_MCP_HTTP_STATELESS=true
FILE_MCP_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=500
ENV
```

```bash
cat > run/env.override <<'ENV'
FILE_MCP_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_S=10
FILE_MCP_CONVERSION_TIMEOUT_S=20
ENV
```

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.prod:/workspace/env.prod:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.override:/workspace/env.override:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.prod,/workspace/env.override \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Precedence:
1. OS environment (`docker run -e ...`)
2. Left-to-right env file list (`FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=file1,file2`)
3. `config.yaml`
4. `defaults.yaml`

## 5. Certificate management (CERTS)

Mount a CA bundle and point runtime to it:

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/certs:/app/certs:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_TLS_CA_BUNDLE=/app/certs/ca.crt \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

The entrypoint installs `FILE_MCP_TLS_CA_BUNDLE` (or `FILE_MCP_STORAGE_TLS_CA_BUNDLE`) into system trust and exports:
- `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`
- `SSL_CERT_FILE`
- `CURL_CA_BUNDLE`

Remote storage backends also support a backend-specific TLS bundle setting:
- `FILE_MCP_STORAGE_TLS_CA_BUNDLE=/app/certs/ca.crt`

To ignore TLS verification errors for remote backends (explicit opt-in):
- `FILE_MCP_STORAGE_TLS_INSECURE=true`

## 5.1 Remote Storage Backends (local|webdav|ftp|s3|google_drive)

Use the same container image and tool surface. Select backend in the env file:

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=webdav
```

WebDAV example:

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=webdav
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_BASE_URL=https://files.example.com/remote.php/dav/files/user/root
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_USERNAME=user
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD=secret
# Optional MOVE resilience controls
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_COUNT=2
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_BACKOFF_S=0.35
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S=5
FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_MOVE_RETRY_STATUSES=408,409,423,425,429,500,502,503,504
```

FTP example:

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=ftp
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_FTP_HOST=ftp.example.com
FILE_MCP_FTP_PORT=21
FILE_MCP_FTP_USERNAME=user
FILE_MCP_FTP_PASSWORD=secret
FILE_MCP_FTP_BASE_DIR=/
FILE_MCP_FTP_USE_TLS=false
```

S3 example:

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=s3
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://storage.example.com
FILE_MCP_S3_BUCKET=my-bucket
FILE_MCP_S3_REGION=us-east-1
FILE_MCP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=...
FILE_MCP_S3_SECRET_KEY=...
FILE_MCP_S3_PREFIX=
```

Google Drive example:

```bash
FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=google_drive
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_FOLDER_ID=1r6kwtGcunVpkbT3nBGmfcWyVfk84_Sjn
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN=...
FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_TOKEN_URI=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
```

### 5.2 Running Each Backend Type (Container, Host Network)

The image is identical for all backends; only the env differs.

1. Local filesystem backend:
```bash
cp docker-env.example run/env.local
sed -i 's/^FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=.*/FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=local/' run/env.local
```
```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-local --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.local:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

2. WebDAV backend:
```bash
cp docker-env.example run/env.webdav
sed -i 's/^FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=.*/FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=webdav/' run/env.webdav
```
Set: `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_BASE_URL`, `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_USERNAME`, `FILE_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD`.

3. FTP backend:
```bash
cp docker-env.example run/env.ftp
sed -i 's/^FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=.*/FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=ftp/' run/env.ftp
```
Set: `FILE_MCP_FTP_HOST`, `FILE_MCP_FTP_USERNAME`, `FILE_MCP_FTP_PASSWORD` (and optional FTP vars).

4. S3 backend:
```bash
cp docker-env.example run/env.s3
sed -i 's/^FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=.*/FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=s3/' run/env.s3
```
Set: `FILE_MCP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `FILE_MCP_S3_BUCKET`, `FILE_MCP_S3_ACCESS_KEY`, `FILE_MCP_S3_SECRET_KEY` (and optional S3 vars).

5. Google Drive backend:
```bash
cp docker-env.example run/env.gdrive
sed -i 's/^FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=.*/FILE_MCP_STORAGE_BACKEND=google_drive/' run/env.gdrive
```
Set: `FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_FOLDER_ID` (or `FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_FOLDER_URL`), `FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID`, `FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET`, and `FILE_MCP_GDRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN`.

Health check (any backend):
```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

## 5.3 Endpoint Health Controls

These env vars configure startup endpoint validation and runtime recovery:
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_ENABLED`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_CHECK_ON_STARTUP`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_CHECK_ALL`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_MAX_RETRIES`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_RETRY_INTERVAL_S`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_RETRY_WINDOW_S`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_MAX_FAILURES_BEFORE_RESTART`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_RECOVER_AFTER_S`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_RESTART_ON_THRESHOLD`
- `FILE_MCP_ENDPOINT_HEALTH_RESTART_EXIT_CODE`

Use MCP tool `backend_status` to inspect current endpoint state.

## 6. Managing and controlling the containerized server

### Foreground (default)

```bash
docker run --rm ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

### Lifecycle control using `server_control.sh` in container

```bash
docker run -d --name file-mcp-server ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest sleep infinity
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  start
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  status
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  stop
```

## 7. Remote Docker host (optional)

Use the same commands with `-H`:

```bash
docker -H tcp://remote-docker-host:2375 run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/workspace:/workspace \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/logs:/workspace/logs \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

## 8. MCP tools available

Core tools exposed through MCP include:
- File IO: `read_file`, `write_file`, `copy_file`, `move_file`, `move_path`, `rename_path`, `delete_file`, `create_dir`, `chmod_path`, `list_dir`
- Search: `search_paths`, `search_content`
- Diff/Base64: `diff_text`, `diff_files`, `b64_encode`, `b64_decode`, `b64_encode_file`, `b64_decode_to_file`
- Validation: `validate_text`, `validate_file`
- Structured edits: JSON/YAML/XML/HTML/Markdown operations, including `*_file` variants
- Conversion and transactional editing: `convert_file`, `sed_edit_file`

## 9. Deploying to production

1. Build and push image:
```bash
./docker-build.sh registry.example.com/cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:2026.02
```
```bash
docker push registry.example.com/cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:2026.02
```
2. Provision host directories for workspace/logs/certs/env.
3. Run container using host network or published ports.
4. Validate:
```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```
5. Validate authenticated MCP call with client integration test.

## 10. Docker-focused test suite

Run command-only tests (no Docker daemon required):

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -k command -q
```

Run container runtime tests (host network) against the built image:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q -rs
```

Run containerized remote storage backend tests (WebDAV/FTP/S3) using `private/env-remote-storage`:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_REMOTE_STORAGE_TESTS=1 \
PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_remote_storage_backends.py -q -rs
```

Run full Docker integration tests locally (`--network=host` and bridge mode):

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 PYTHONPATH=src \
pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```

Enable optional bridge publish validation:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_BRIDGE_TESTS=1 PYTHONPATH=src \
pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```

Run against remote Docker host:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 \
FILE_MCP_DOCKER_HOST=tcp://remote-docker-host:2375 \
PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```
